<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="031" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>ReadableColumns additions (UAC review) + Information section fields (FR-18)</title>
    <phase>3 Grids, information, messages</phase>
    <gate>after 028 and 030 (030's final column list and owner answers recorded)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include bff-api and authorization; changes the external column allow-list (a security boundary) and .tsx code</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The allow-list is the external security boundary; each column is a disclosure decision with UAC review</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>C</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>028, 030</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, frontend, react, authorization, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add exactly the columns task 030 verified and the owner approved to the external modules' ReadableColumns, with UAC's review recorded, and show them in each record type's Information section; prove an unlisted column is still refused.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. ASP.NET Core Minimal API and external-access authorization developer; React developer for the SPA.</role>
  <goal>Each type's Information section renders its approved fields (lookups by formatted name); every new column is on its module's `ReadableColumns` with a comment citing FR-18 and the UAC review; the regression test proves an unlisted column is still refused.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-18, SC-3, NFR-04. The external module fetch refuses any column outside the module's `ReadableColumns` with 400 `DV_FETCHXML_COLUMN_NOT_PERMITTED` / `DV_RECORD_COLUMN_NOT_PERMITTED` (`RecordDetailFields.tsx:8-12`). Allow-list blocks (verified 2026-11-10, `ExternalAccessModule.cs`): project `:450-455`, invoice `:528-539`, work assignment `:556-562`, matter `:580-585` (documents `:494-501`, service request `:830-833`). UAC task 157 trimmed the lists to grid columns (rule (b)); a non-grid column carries a stated reason, as the invoice `statuscode` entry does (`:532-536`). The Information section reads one row through the id-filtered module fetch and prefers `@formattedValues` (`RecordDetailFields.tsx:14-21`, `formatDetailValue` `:201-226`); the fetch seam is `Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalModuleDataEndpoints.cs`. The column list comes ONLY from `notes/task-030-information-fields.md`. ebilling adds `sprk_reviewdetail` to the same invoice block (082c-2), so the invoice block is a merge hot spot.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalModuleDataEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/ExternalModuleColumnAllowListTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">The per-type RecordTemplateConfig (task 003) and the Information section renderer (task 005) under src/client/external-spa/src/components/detail/</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/components/detail/RecordDetailFields.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/tests/RecordDetailModal.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/notes/task-030-information-fields.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="028" status="pending">P2 deployed (phase-deploy convention)</dependency>
      <dependency task="030" status="pending">Verified, owner-approved column list</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec FR-18 MUST">Every column this task adds to any `ReadableColumns` set comes from task 030's final list, carries a code comment naming spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4 task 031, FR-18 ("NOT grid-derived: Information section") and the UAC review reference, and has UAC's review recorded in the PR before merge.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">No `sprk_signal` column, no pointer column (sprk_graphdriveid/itemid/filepath), and no column 030 marked NOT FOUND or field-secured-without-decision is added. Removing or reordering existing entries is out of scope.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec FR-18">Lookups render the formatted name from `@formattedValues` without reading the `_ref` entity; confirm in `ExternalModuleDataEndpoints.cs` that the module fetch returns it for the added lookups and cite file:line in the notes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010, NFR-05">No new DI registration, interface, package or route; this is a data change to existing descriptors.</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions">State the Placement Justification in the PR (cite `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`: extends the existing external allow-list). Measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build (short paths, same zip tool, matching file counts); ≥ +5 MB needs justification; total ≤ 60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR: `ExternalAccessModule.cs` is shared with unified-access-control-r2 and ebilling-r1. Never deploy the dev BFF directly; the deploy is requested through uac-r2 in task 038 (`docs/procedures/dev-bff-deploy-coordination.md`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Integration tests at the KEEP path `tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/`; no banned mocks. Must-fire: each added column reads. Must-not-fire: a column still not on the list is refused with 400 and its errorCode.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 A1">Data access stays app-only and Tier-2-scoped; the change adds readable columns only, never widens row scope.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/spec.md</file>
