    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Non-grid allow-list entry with a reason" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs">invoice `statuscode` entry and comment at :532-536</pattern>
      <pattern name="Field row config" location="src/client/external-spa/src/components/detail/RecordDetailFields.tsx">DetailFieldDef { attribute, label, kind } per type</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load the knowledge files, read the relevant files, declare rigor and model tier per task-execute Step 0.5.</step>
    <step order="1">Read task 030's final list; for each lookup, confirm from `ExternalModuleDataEndpoints.cs` that `@formattedValues` carries the name; note file:line.</step>
    <step order="2">Write the failing tests first in `ExternalModuleColumnAllowListTests.cs`: each new column reads through the module fetch (must-fire); a representative unlisted column (e.g. `ownerid`) is still refused with 400 and its errorCode (must-not-fire).</step>
    <step order="3">Add the columns to the module `ReadableColumns` sets with the required comments.</step>
    <step order="4">Seeding proof for the refusal guard: temporarily add the probe column to the list, confirm the must-not-fire test fails, restore; record it in the notes.</step>
    <step order="5">Add the field rows (label, kind) to each type's Information config; lookups use kind `lookup` and render the formatted name; empty shows the em dash.</step>
    <step order="6">SPA tests: each type's Information section renders the new fields; a lookup with only a formatted value renders its name and never a GUID.</step>
    <step order="7">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/`, the integration tests filtered to ExternalModuleColumnAllowList (tests under tests/integration/auth/** compile into tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests; filter there, and re-run any failure in isolation — R3 gotcha on machine load), the SPA tests and build; measure publish size per bff-hygiene and record it.</step>
    <step order="8">Prepare the UAC review request (columns, reason, disclosure of internal names) and record UAC's answer in the notes and PR.</step>
    <step order="9">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` and this POML's &lt;status&gt; to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1`.</step>
    <step order="10">Record deviations, measurements and the UAC review in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/notes/task-031-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If UAC declines a column, drop it from both the allow-list and the Information config and tell the owner; never ship a column without the recorded review.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a lookup's formatted name would require reading the referenced entity (a new read or a `_ref` table on the allow-list), STOP and escalate rather than adding that read.</trigger>
    <trigger>If ebilling's or uac-r2's open work changes the same `ReadableColumns` blocks, STOP and coordinate through `/conflict-check` before merging.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>The external allow-lists in `ExternalAccessModule.cs` (:450-455, :528-539, :556-562, :580-585) and the field config `RECORD_DETAIL_ENTITIES` (`RecordDetailFields.tsx:73-171`).</existing>
    <extension>Yes — this task extends both existing lists; it adds no new component, route or registration.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The Information section cannot show the fields partners need (matter description, practice area, responsible people), and the module fetch refuses them with 400 if the SPA asks.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Information fields per type">
      <url>https://{spa-dev-host}/?record=matter:{matter-id}</url>
      <steps>
        <step>Open a matter, a project, a work assignment and an invoice</step>
        <step>Verify each approved field shows a value or an em dash; lookups show a name, never a GUID</step>
        <step>Check the console and network for 400 DV_*_COLUMN_NOT_PERMITTED</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All approved fields render; no 400s</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps><step>Switch to dark and high-contrast</step><step>Verify the Information labels and values adapt</step></steps>
      <expected>Semantic tokens only</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Run SPA tests and build</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/external-spa/src/components/detail/RecordDetailFields.tsx</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/ExternalModuleColumnAllowListTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/external-spa/tests/RecordDetailModal.test.tsx</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/notes/task-031-notes.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Every column on task 030's final list is on its module's `ReadableColumns` with the required comment, and no other column was added.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Must-fire: an integration test reads each added column through the external module fetch successfully.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Must-not-fire: a column not on the list is still refused with 400 and its `errorCode`; the seeding proof is recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each type's Information section renders the approved fields; lookups show the formatted name and never a GUID; empty values show the em dash.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No `sprk_signal` column, pointer column, new route, DI registration or package is added.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">UAC's review is recorded in the task notes and cited in the PR.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF build is green; the filtered integration tests and the SPA tests pass; publish size is recorded, ≤ 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-18, SC-3, NFR-04/05. Design §5's allow-list line numbers (:385-388 etc.) are stale; use the ones above. Adversarial review: two passes (authorization). Deploy: task 038 via uac-r2.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
